null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:27:00Z", "username": "Lzafeer Ahmad B F", "text": "And it indeed had a common etymology!", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:27:16Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Ye padhna padhega", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:28:22Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Ye kahin aur mat bolna please 🙈", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:29:06Z", "username": "Dr.Namrata Srinivasan", "text": "Y?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:29:07Z", "username": "Lzafeer Ahmad B F", "text": "tareef was description. Came to be used in trade where goods would be described along with price. so from there tareef became tariff for the price.", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:29:35Z", "username": "Dr.Namrata Srinivasan", "text": "Is it the same tareef as in praise?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:30:02Z", "username": "Lzafeer Ahmad B F", "text": "Yep!", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:30:17Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Ganja fukne wala circle chota hi acha.\nKuch logo ko zarurat nhi hai pehle hi kaafi BT mein rehte hain 😂🙈", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:30:45Z", "username": "Sidhesh K K", "text": "So the song..\nAur das kitniya tarifan chaidiye tenu... was a prediction on Donny", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:30:59Z", "username": "Lzafeer Ahmad B F", "text": "THats why the usage was “aapki tareef” when asking someone who they are. Because tareef was literally description", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:31:41Z", "username": "Dr.Namrata Srinivasan", "text": "Oh crazy", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:31:48Z", "username": "Dr.Namrata Srinivasan", "text": "So could be negative also but usually positive", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:32:06Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "I believe the meaning of “praise” is only present in Farsi and Hindustani — not in Arabic", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:32:19Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "in Arabic the meaning still is identification/notification/description", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:32:52Z", "username": "Dr.Namrata Srinivasan", "text": "Maybe it was something that got associated with “positive description “", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:32:54Z", "username": "Lzafeer Ahmad B F", "text": "YEs. The hindi tareef is derivative of Arabic one. IIRC", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:33:13Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "yes, that’s what i remember reading too", "role": "confirmation", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:33:48Z", "username": "Akshay", "text": "Superb q!", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:33:53Z", "username": "Anurag Bhide", "text": "In formal Hindi or Urdu I guess they use \"aapki tareef?\" to mean who are you?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:33:55Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "A question because I just want to share a trippy video", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:34:12Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Q. It is a common misconception that all Xs fall over when they are excited, but the phenomenon is actually specific to a single breed: the Myotonic X, more popularly known as the \"Fainting X.\"\nThe \"fainting\" isn't actually a loss of consciousness or a result of being tired; it is a hereditary genetic condition called myotonia congenita. Because the muscles stiffen so suddenly, the X loses its balance. If the X is standing still, it might just stiffen like a board and tip over sideways. If it is running when the \"faint\" occurs, its legs lock up, and momentum causes it to tumble. Id X", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:34:21Z", "username": "Lzafeer Ahmad B F", "text": "Trippy in the trippy sense or the Stevie G trippy sense", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:34:29Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Hahahahhaa both 😂", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:34:40Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "You'll get when you see the video 😂", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:34:41Z", "username": "Pavan Pamidimarri", "text": "goats", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-03-04T17:34:48Z", "username": "Anurag Bhide", "text": "Horse?", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]